---
description: Keep code comments rare and only for non-obvious logic
alwaysApply: true
---

# Comments

- Comment only to explain **non-obvious / complex logic** (why, not what).
- Never comment types, props, exports, or restatements of the next line.
- Prefer **1–2 lines**. Use at most **3–4 lines** when the invariant truly needs it.
- Do not paste design-discussion or plan prose into the codebase.
- If the code is clear with a good name, add **no** comment.
